      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A case of diaphragm-like stricture of the colon induced by non steroidal anti-inflammatory drug (diclofénac LP) is reported in a 65-year-old man who presented abdominal pain. Colonoscopy revealed ulcer in the transverse right colon. The patient gradually developed diaphragm-like stricture in the transverse right colon. A right hemicolectomy was performed."},
